    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d578-a1">

                <pb facs="1040" n="946" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg946"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 95.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Vlangally to Mr. Lothrop.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Asiatic Department, No</hi>. 79</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1887-01-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 8–20, 1887</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Envoy</hi>: In consequence of the note addressed
                    by you to me on the 10–20 of December, I hastened to ask information of the
                    maritime province, by telegraph, in regard to the seizure of the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Henrietta.</hi></p>
                <p>I have now the honor to bring to your knowledge that, according to the
                    information communicated to mo by General Enghelm, acting governor of said
                    province, the <hi rendition="#italic">Henrietta</hi> was in fact seized and
                    confiscated on the 17–29 August, in virtue of a decision of the commission
                    sitting on board of the imperial corvette <hi rendition="#italic">Kreysser</hi>,
                    for the offense of illicit trading on our coasts.</p>
                <p>Pray accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">A. Vlangally.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
